# tax/3 — the whole liability

> Module SaraTax

> Using SaraWorld as W
> Using SaraKinship as K
> Using Section1 as S1
> Using Section3306 as S3306

`utils.pl` closes the corpus with

```prolog
tax(Taxp,Taxy,Tax) :-
    ( s1(Taxp,Taxy,_,Income_tax) ; (\+ s1(Taxp,Taxy,_,_), Income_tax is 0) ),
    ( s3301(Taxp,Taxy,_,_,_,Employment_tax)
    ; (\+ s3301(Taxp,Taxy,_,_,_,_), Employment_tax is 0) ),
    Tax is Income_tax+Employment_tax.
```

which is the income tax of §1 plus the unemployment excise of §3301, each
falling back to zero where the section does not apply. Both are read at their
*first* solution, because `Income_tax` and `Employment_tax` arrive unbound and
the conjunction never backtracks into them — nothing after them can fail except
the final arithmetic, which cannot.

One hundred of the 376 cases end here, and they are the only ones that ask for
a number rather than a verdict.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope Total:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  ## §1
  output income_tax content money
  ## §3301
  output employment_tax content money
  output total content money
```

```catala
scope Total:
  definition income_tax equals
    (output of S1.Tax with {
       -- world: world -- injections: injections -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
       -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
       -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
       -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
       -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
       -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).tax

  definition employment_tax equals
    if not (output of S3306.UnemploymentTax with {
              -- world: world -- injections: injections
              -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
              -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
              -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
              -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
              -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of
              -- employer: taxpayer -- caly: taxable_year }).holds
    then $0
    else (output of S3306.UnemploymentTax with {
            -- world: world -- injections: injections
            -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
            -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
            -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
            -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
            -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of
            -- employer: taxpayer -- caly: taxable_year }).tax

  definition total equals income_tax + employment_tax
```
